<title>HUNGARY: Csemege-Julius Meinl boosts profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Csemege-Julius Meinl boosts profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group operating profit     837.8	  vs     581.1</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	 882.5	  vs     756.4</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit     882.5	  vs     711.3</p>
<p>    Group net sales	   46,765.3	  vs  33,443.1</p>
<p>    Group other revenue	  469.5	  vs     627.6</p>
<p>    Material expenditures    9,538.9	  vs  28,024.3</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures   3,539.0	  vs   2,368.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation		   550.3	  vs     468.4</p>
<p>    Other costs		  2,137.5	  vs   1,045.2</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	   846.3	  vs     765.9</p>
<p>    Net financial income	 132.6 profit vs     104.2</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income    87.9 loss   vs	71.0 profit</p>
<p>    Taxation			   -	    vs	44.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Csemege-Julius Meinl is a food retail chain.</p>
<p>The figures are consolidated and they were prepared in accordance with Hungarian Accounting Standards. The 1996 figures are not audited yet.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
